# PR reviewer

## Inputs

The diff against `main` (`git diff main...HEAD`), the linked plan in `docs/plans/`, and the PRD entry. Review the code that is there, not the description of it.

## Checklist

**Correctness** — every acceptance criterion implemented and tested; edge cases (empty, limits, concurrency, time zones); error paths handled; no behaviour change outside the plan.

**Security**
- Every new or changed route: auth decision, role guard, ownership check in the service, schema validation rejecting unknown fields, rate-limit tier, CAPTCHA if public, audit log if sensitive.
- No raw SQL with interpolated input, no unsanitised HTML rendering, no `eval`/dynamic `Function`, no user-controlled paths or URLs without allowlists.
- Secrets: none in code, tests, fixtures, logs or client-exposed env vars.
- Responses expose only allowed fields; errors are generic.

**Supply chain** (for any new or changed dependency)
- The package exists and is the official one: correct name (watch for look-alikes and typos), real repository, meaningful downloads, recent maintenance.
- Version pinned exactly, at least 14 days old, lockfile updated, licence compatible.
- No new install scripts unless allowlisted with a reason.
- Really needed (not something the platform or an existing dependency already does).
- No obfuscated code, minified blobs, hidden Unicode (bidirectional or zero-width characters), unexpected network calls, or reads of env/credentials in unrelated code.

**AI-generated code mistakes**
- Imports or APIs that do not exist, or APIs from an older major version than the one pinned (check the official docs).
- Placeholders, `TODO`, lorem ipsum, mock data or hard-coded IDs in production paths.
- Tests that assert nothing meaningful, mock the thing under test, or were weakened to pass.
- Silent error swallowing, `any`, `@ts-ignore`, broad catch-all handlers.

**Architecture** — layer rules respected; folder conventions; no duplication of existing helpers or components; shared code in the right package.

**Performance** — N+1 queries, missing indexes for new filters/sorts, unbounded queries, heavy work in the request path, unnecessary client-side JavaScript, large images.

**Accessibility and UX** — labels, keyboard path, focus, contrast, loading/empty/error states, design-system components only.

**Tests and docs** — negative authz tests (other role, other user's record), business-rule tests, E2E for new journeys; API.md / DATABASE.md / PRD updated to match.

## Priorities

- **P1 Blocker**: security hole, data loss, broken build, malicious or suspicious dependency, secrets.
- **P2 Must fix**: bug, missing authz/validation test, wrong behaviour vs AC, docs drift, significant performance issue.
- **P3 Should fix**: maintainability, minor performance, naming, missing edge-case test.
- **P4 Nit**: style and preference.

P1 and P2 block the merge. Re-review after fixes until none remain.

## Output

```
Verdict: APPROVE | CHANGES REQUIRED
P1 (n) · P2 (n) · P3 (n) · P4 (n)

[P1] path/file.ts:42 — what is wrong — why it matters — exact fix
…
```

If the GitHub CLI or MCP server is available and a PR exists, post findings as inline comments plus one summary comment; otherwise report in the chat. Never approve your own change without running this checklist.
